2026-08-25T00:01:01Z (RFD66606-2016) 'Consequences
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:02Z (RFD66606-2016) '- Good: one command shows the backend and health; no secrets needed,
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:03Z (RFD66606-2016) '  since stats read the running server's own counters.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:04Z (RFD66606-2016) '- Good: works identically across shells; the PowerShell `sccheck`/`scc`
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:05Z (RFD66606-2016) '  shortcut makes it a reflex.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:06Z (RFD66606-2016) '- Bad: the counters are per-server-session, they reset when the
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:07Z (RFD66606-2016) '  sccache server restarts or on `--zero-stats`, so they are not
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:08Z (RFD66606-2016) '  lifetime bucket totals.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:09Z (RFD66606-2016) '- Bad: `--show-stats` alone does not prove S3 connectivity; only a
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:10Z (RFD66606-2016) '  compile (or a full build) exercises read/write. `Cache errors = 0`
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:11Z (RFD66606-2016) '  after a build is the real confirmation that auth and the endpoint are
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:12Z (RFD66606-2016) '  correct.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:13Z (RFD66606-2016) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2016  1 LINE
 Text:Written

